# Settings ▸ Tabs ▸ "Hide the toolbar until you need it" (not in Arc), at rest. The browser window looked at the
# pointer 20 times a second while the bar floated, so a frontmost Cra woke 20 times a second with the pointer
# resting mid-page. The shell's tracking area now samples the pointer as it moves, and the only timer is a
# one-shot look the tracker asks for (the wait in the strip, the delay before the bar goes). `toolbar=move`
# samples a stand-in pointer as a move does (the real pointer of a scenario's copy can be anywhere), and
# `toolbar=timers:<label>` counts the looks the timer took since the last `timers`.
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": true, "autoHideToolbar": true}
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=idle
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 2
# Parked mid-page with the bar away: nothing waits, and nothing wakes while the pointer rests.
cra://debug?toolbar=move:700,400
expect-log toolbar move:700,400: out=0 look=0
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:1
wait 2
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:2
expect-log toolbar timers:2: out=0 look=0 looks=0
# To the top edge: one look after the dwell brings the bar out.
cra://debug?toolbar=move:700,4
expect-log toolbar move:700,4: out=0 look=1
wait 0.5
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:3
expect-log toolbar timers:3: out=1 look=0 looks=1
# Resting on the bar: still out, and nothing wakes.
wait 2
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:4
expect-log toolbar timers:4: out=1 look=0 looks=0
# Back to the middle of the page: one look after the delay takes the bar away, then nothing again.
cra://debug?toolbar=move:700,400
expect-log toolbar move:700,400: out=1 look=1
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:5
expect-log toolbar timers:5: out=0 look=0 looks=1
wait 2
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:6
expect-log toolbar timers:6: out=0 look=0 looks=0
# Out through the window's top edge: 2 pt above the window is still the strip's band, which keeps the bar, and no
# move comes from up there. The bar used to stay out until the pointer came back; it is looked at again while
# the pointer is in the band, and goes once the pointer is further out.
cra://debug?toolbar=move:700,4
wait 0.5
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:7
expect-log toolbar timers:7: out=1 look=0 looks=1
cra://debug?toolbar=move:700,-2
expect-log toolbar move:700,-2: out=1 look=1
wait 0.5
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:8
expect-log toolbar timers:8: out=1 look=1 looks=[1-9][0-9]*
cra://debug?toolbar=move:700,-40
expect-log toolbar move:700,-40: out=1 look=1
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:9
expect-log toolbar timers:9: out=0 look=0 looks=[1-9][0-9]*
wait 2
cra://debug?toolbar=timers:10
expect-log toolbar timers:10: out=0 look=0 looks=0
cra://debug?toolbar=gone
expect-log toolbar gone: floats=1 out=0 inset=0 page=[0-9]+/[0-9]+ short=0 barHidden=1 look=0
